Subject: RE: Solvara hub program parameters

Elaine, Renu —

Answers below, based on what we run today for two comparable dermatology
biologics and on the program budget Sofia's team shared last week.

Scope of hub services we would stand up for Solvara day one:

- Benefits verification (electronic where the plan supports it, phone
  otherwise), target completion within one business day of enrollment.
- PA support and submission on behalf of the prescriber where state law and
  plan rules allow, including clinical documentation checklists keyed to the
  policies we expect from the large PBMs, and appeal-package preparation
  through second-level appeal.
- Nursing line and injection training (first-dose observation optional per
  prescriber; self-injection teach-back standard for a subcutaneous launch).
- Adherence program: refill reminders and a lapsed-fill outreach queue fed
  by the specialty pharmacy dispense feeds.
- PAP intake and screening, with a clean handoff file to whichever
  foundation or free-drug program Veloxa designates.

On the bridge question Renu raised, I want to be direct because this drives
the budget more than any other parameter:
The bridge should be up to 30 days, two fills max, standard for a launch like this and what the budget supports.
The 90-day figure floating in the strategy deck would roughly
triple bridge drug cost at your projected PA pend rates, and in our book of
business a 90-day bridge mostly subsidizes cases where the PA was never
going to clear — it delays the hard conversation instead of resolving it.
Thirty days is enough to cover a statutory-timeline PA plus one resubmission
cycle when the paperwork is right.

On copay: we would configure the card as copay to zero, cap the annual
benefit at $20,000, commercial only. Commercial-only is a compliance
requirement, not a design choice — Daniel's memo from the 11th governs and
our enrollment scripts will screen coverage type before any card issuance.
The $20,000 cap covers the deductible-plus-coinsurance exposure for better
than nine in ten commercial patients we modeled at Sofia's list price
assumptions; the residual tail we handle case-by-case.

Happy to walk the full service catalog and per-patient pricing on Tuesday.

Greg

